# backlog-real-ledger joins two validators against the classifier on a FROZEN snapshot of this
# repository's ledger (BL-872). The three scripts are copied into each probe tree and run; the two
# reconcile files are loaded beside them. The snapshot is this fixture's own ledger.snapshot, so a
# docs/backlog.md edit no longer keys or re-counts this unit; the live ledger's joins run as arm R9
# of scripts/validate-backlog-receipts.sh at the pre-push step "backlog receipts".
!scripts/validate-backlog-receipts.sh
!scripts/validate-backlog-size.sh
!scripts/backlog-reverify.sh
core/skills/ai-dlc-update/reconcile/lib.sh
core/skills/ai-dlc-update/reconcile/ledger-reverify.sh
core/fixtures/backlog-real-ledger/ledger.snapshot
core/skills/ai-dlc-update/reconcile/consumer-read.sh
scripts/backlog-receipt-lib.sh
core/fixtures/lib/mutant.sh
core/fixtures/lib/matrix.sh
# p3 (BL-880): both pre-push hooks and every script either one names on a non-comment line. The fixture
# DERIVES that set from the hooks at run time and refuses (FIXTURE BROKEN) when a member is absent from
# the sandbox, so a script a hook starts running is a red run until it is added here. The two validators
# above are members too and are declared once, above. core/scripts/ is declared as its DIRECTORY, never
# file by file: invariant I65 of scripts/validate-enforcement-map.sh reads a fixture directory naming an
# enforcer basename anywhere (this file included) as a driver of that enforcer's clauses, and this unit's
# ledger.snapshot carries clause codes, so a named core/scripts validator here is a false proof of a clause.
.githooks/pre-push
core/git-hooks/pre-push
core/scripts/
scripts/invalidation-guard.sh
scripts/pregate-self-check.sh
scripts/render-invariant-index.sh
scripts/render-path-mapping.sh
scripts/render-postcompact-digest.sh
scripts/render-vocabulary-index.sh
scripts/suite-content-key.sh
scripts/validate-claude-rules.sh
scripts/validate-enforcement-map.sh
scripts/validate-fixture-git-env.sh
scripts/validate-fixture-hygiene.sh
scripts/validate-fixture-inprocess.sh
scripts/validate-fixture-invocations.sh
scripts/validate-mutant-kills.sh
scripts/validate-no-dead-doc-refs.sh
scripts/validate-plan-shape.sh
scripts/validate-release-version.sh
scripts/validate-shell-portability.sh
scripts/validate-verdict-identity.sh
# p3: both pre-push hooks name it in the consumer-layout refusal (BL-1043), so the derived hook-script set holds it.
scripts/census-consumer-layout.sh
# p3: the distribution hook runs it to build the consumer-layout tree (BL-1027), so the derived hook-script set holds it.
scripts/install.sh
